#NEXUS

[ martínez2017a_fig11: Vertical time tree, read by measuring the horizontal node bars and the stems (box edges) that meet them in the image. One trichotomy: Co. rhodesiensis, Camposaurus and Lucianovenator meet one bar. Theropoda (on the node above Sauropodomorpha), Neotheropoda and Coelophysidae (joined to its node by a curved arrow) are kept as labels. The range boxes, maps and arrows of Sauropodomorpha and Averostra are not branches. 17 tips, 1 polytomies (3 children); 3 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 9 case (census 3, seed 20261272). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

